<description>&lt;p&gt;Mozambique's security forces suffered a setback in Cabo Delgado as they lost a key counter-insurgency battle, while the government continues its December deadline for civilians to surrender illegal firearms and has killed another Anamola group member. Rwanda warned it will pull its troops from Mozambique unless sustainable funding is provided, adding pressure on the joint effort against the insurgents. Mozambique is also seeking an India partnership to boost agro-processing and expand rice trade across Southern Africa. The insurgency caused 151 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxPSllqczNaZVNZN2ZPY3ZmWEpITmh2aFBXdGlMYS1rcC1oSm5nM3owYkF3c1FNbDdCZ3Z1NkNJNlJZTHVKWndXY0NJTWc0dlpDUFJsS2ZxRGFfX3NlNTltbDNpZEpSdXMtbjRDWDFSbHRIOVJvOV9wUW8xWjd4aks0LVctWUlwVENsOWhESE9RUzBaUTIxMDZBV0JFUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Mail &amp;amp; Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxPcnBfajdBQ3R3SllYS1NMQnFicXk5YkFBejVlLTJoOGl4TjVucWh3WVJpS1MwNlUwZzBkOXBlR0F4TG9lUzR1Ny14dnYwY2dmRXRpcHloZXI3QWgwT2VCbnZidDFPVVBFNXhfai1OYkJ1TWdiNnRvOFExMVZibE93YkdwM25rUzFkWjg0Q09scTRrTkVFQWYwcm9CZjdDeHBnYThQV0ZvQkFqQVRTRENPa0wyOGZvNl9DZDA1Zg?oc=5&quot;&gt;SOCRadar&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxPdUxaNGRGLXdKZlBRaFFRdXdDZERlVW9VMm5IUWdwVVU5N0FyR1lEblBPYWN5QnZaUUl5ZzNycjJCS09NR3k5V2w5cDM4bjIxNzFBYjZ0c1o2RHNSX1lrdHZBbzI2RktQSkxtLUltM1VqZ3NrbHZSbF80M1VFWkhDSUc5QUtHT2Y5VTF6Tjl1aTJXOTVzd19EOXJVWGNHUXRfcTMxdnFkS0VDenhxeXRJcUc0d3I?oc=5&quot;&gt;UG Diplomat&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxQb3M4ckN2cXJnMVctdmxhWDlCUnZPODRaQURjWWxLTXpSTVVZdUhRc29VUkhRLURuOE9fOGlTeGM1dW5Ib2hCdlB5